Explanation of the change:

- Original: `/\w+:(?!:)/` only matches one or more “word” characters (`[A-Za-z0-9_]`) followed by a single `:`, excluding the `::` operator.  
- New:      `/\w+\??:(?!:)/` allows an optional `?` (`\??`) just before the `:`, so both `foo:`, `foo?:` are recognized as attribute names, but still not `::`.
